      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-04T10:44:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why does dex2oatd crash?",
      "parentUuid": "8549c87c_218ef429",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 47,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 99
      },
      "revId": "24496f9d172fdbcc9f59d595c505fcee2e539ff4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3ee18445_7bfcec7c",
        "filename": "runtime/interpreter/interpreter_cache.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 24,
      "author": {
        "id": 1258954
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-04T16:45:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`IsSuspended()` is true with the thread is not runnable and suspend-request flag is set. In CMC, we are calling Clear() during thread-flip. At that time, if gc-thread runs it for some mutator then mutator is guaranteed to be not runnable. But I believe it also doesn\u0027t have suspend-request flag set as we free all threads to be able to finish their flip-function and then become runnable.\n\nSo either IsSuspended() has to be updated or this DCHECK has to be adjusted. I believe something like what I suggested in my comment above makes sense.\n\ndex2oatd on boot-image is failing because that\u0027s the first thing during build that triggers GC. Otheriwse nothing special about it.",
      "parentUuid": "84c8c96d_87bfb609",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 47,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 99
      },
      "revId": "24496f9d172fdbcc9f59d595c505fcee2e539ff4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ed95971_0e477c11",
        "filename": "runtime/interpreter/interpreter_cache.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 24,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042828
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-05T01:44:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the problematic case, I think kRunningFlipFunction should be set, and won\u0027t be cleared until we do so, right? So can we say owning_thread-\u003eIsSuspended() || owning_thread-\u003eReadFlag(ThreadFlag::kRunningFlipFunction, std::memory_order_relaxed) ?",
      "parentUuid": "3ee18445_7bfcec7c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 47,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 99
      },
      "revId": "24496f9d172fdbcc9f59d595c505fcee2e539ff4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fc835389_d5830a23",
        "filename": "runtime/interpreter/interpreter_cache.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 24,
      "author": {
        "id": 1258954
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-05T15:05:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes that\u0027s what I was thinking. But additionally, is it possible to assert that self is the thread running that flip-function on the owning-thread? Because otherwise, we could have thread1 running flip-function on owning-thread, and thread2 calling Clear() (we don\u0027t do that anywhere of course), and in that case also owning-thread can become runnable anytime, right?",
      "parentUuid": "6ed95971_0e477c11",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 47,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 99
      },
      "revId": "24496f9d172fdbcc9f59d595c505fcee2e539ff4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "90dbe6ea_34a25e09",
        "filename": "runtime/interpreter/interpreter_cache.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 24,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042828
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-05T22:31:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think there\u0027s currently a way to tell that. But I expect scale will save us here. I think if that happened, we might miss those failures, but we will see others, where the flip-function just finished. You can make a similar argument about the current code, but it seems far less likely to me that we would consistently encounter the other thread running a flip-function than that we would consistently see it in a suspended state.",
      "parentUuid": "fc835389_d5830a23",
